    "contentMarkdown": "# Веб-доступність за ADA\n\nВебдоступність за ADA (ADA Web Accessibility) — це забезпечення рівного доступу людей з інвалідністю до цифрових послуг відповідно до вимог американського Закону про захист прав людей з інвалідністю (Americans with Disabilities Act). Розділ II (Title II) регламентує діяльність державних органів і місцевого самоврядування США, тоді як Розділ III (Title III) поширюється на комерційні компанії та некомерційні організації, що вважаються публічними просторами.\n\n## How do Title II and Title III differ?\n\n| ADA title | Web accessibility requirements |\n|---|---|\n| **Title II** | The U.S. Department of Justice rule sets WCAG 2.1 Level AA as the technical standard for covered web content and mobile apps that state and local governments provide or make available, including through relevant vendor arrangements. The rule specifies exceptions and other conditions. |\n| **Title III** | The Department of Justice’s web guidance explains that covered public accommodations must make the goods and services they offer online accessible. Use WCAG as a technical benchmark and evaluate the obligations that apply to the business. |\n\n## What are the ADA Title II web rule deadlines?\n\nUnder the April 2026 interim final rule, state and local government entities with a population of 50,000 or more, excluding special districts, have until **April 26, 2027**. Entities below 50,000 and special district governments have until **April 26, 2028**. Existing Title II obligations continue to apply before these dates.\n\n## What should a product team do?\n\nFor a city’s online permit application, include the portal, its forms, and the submission and payment steps in the accessibility scope. Identify any applicable exceptions, then evaluate the covered process against WCAG 2.1 AA. For a private retailer, start with the scope of Title III and the applicable legal context. Use WCAG to turn barriers in browsing and checkout into testable findings. [Section 508](/ua/glossary/section-508.html) is a separate federal ICT framework relevant to U.S. federal agencies and the products they procure.\n\n## Пов'язані терміни\n\n- [Accessibility and WCAG](/ua/glossary/accessibility-wcag.html)\n- [Section 508](/ua/glossary/section-508.html)\n- [Web Accessibility Audit](/ua/glossary/web-accessibility-audit.html)\n- [European Accessibility Act (EAA)](/ua/glossary/european-accessibility-act.html)\n\n## Джерела\n\n- [Guidance on Web Accessibility and the ADA, U.S. Department of Justice](https://www.ada.gov/resources/web-guidance/)\n- [ADA Title III Regulations, U.S. Department of Justice](https://www.ada.gov/law-and-regs/regulations/title-iii-regulations/)\n- [28 CFR § 35.200, Electronic Code of Federal Regulations](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-28/chapter-I/part-35/subpart-H/section-35.200)\n- [2026 Interim Final Rule Extending Compliance Dates, Federal Register](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-04-20/pdf/2026-07663.pdf)\n- [Title II Small Entity Compliance Guide, U.S. Department of Justice](https://www.ada.gov/resources/small-entity-compliance-guide/)",
