    "seoTitle": "Дизайн за підтримки ШІ (AI-Assisted Design) | Словник продуктового дизайну — Lex Konovalov",
    "seoDescription": "Дизайн за підтримки ШІ (AI-assisted Design) — це використання інструментів штучного інтелекту на окремих етапах процесу дизайну, як-от генерація варіантів, підготовка контенту чи побудова прототипів. При цьому дизайнер зберігає відповідальність за визначення проблеми та оцінку отриманого результату.",
    "canonicalUrl": "https://lexkonovalov.com/ua/glossary/ai-assisted-design.html",
    "sources": [
      "Design Process Isn't Dead, It's Compressed, NN/g (https://www.nngroup.com/articles/design-process-isnt-dead/)",
      "AI Prototyping in Real Design Contexts, NN/g (https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ai-prototyping/)"
    ],
    "contentMarkdown": "# Дизайн за підтримки ШІ (AI-Assisted Design)\n\nДизайн за підтримки ШІ (AI-assisted Design) — це використання інструментів штучного інтелекту на окремих етапах процесу дизайну, як-от генерація варіантів, підготовка контенту чи побудова прототипів. При цьому дизайнер зберігає відповідальність за визначення проблеми та оцінку отриманого результату.\n\n## Designing with AI vs. designing an AI product\n\n**AI-assisted design** describes how the work is done. **[AI-native design](/ua/glossary/ai-native-design.html)** concerns products whose experience depends substantially on AI capabilities.\n\nA designer can use AI to prototype a conventional settings page. A team can also design an AI assistant using sketches and ordinary prototyping tools. These are different dimensions of the work.\n\n## Where can AI help a designer?\n\n| Task | Useful contribution | What still needs judgment |\n|---|---|---|\n| Explore alternatives | Draft different layouts or approaches | Whether they address a real need |\n| Write interface content | Suggest labels and error messages | Accuracy, tone, and the actual recovery path |\n| Build a prototype | Implement a specified interaction | Whether the behavior represents the idea being tested |\n| Review a design | Identify possible omissions | Whether each finding is supported and important |\n\nTreat generated alternatives as proposals. Repetition across several responses is not independent evidence.\n\n## Example: an operations dashboard\n\nSuppose a designer has identified the core objects, statuses, and relationships in a booking workflow. They give an agent that model, representative content, and the shared component references.\n\nThe agent builds a prototype with sorting and filtering. The designer checks whether the filters refer to the right objects, whether important exceptions remain visible, and whether the UI fits the actual task.\n\nStarting from a verified [object model](/ua/glossary/object-mapping.html) gives the prototype a clearer structure. It does not establish that users will understand or value the proposed dashboard.\n\n## A practical AI-assisted workflow\n\nDefine the question and constraints first. Supply the evidence, source material, component references, and examples needed for that question. Ask for a bounded deliverable that can be inspected.\n\nReview the result against the brief. Check factual claims against sources, behavior against requirements, and implementation against the real component API. Revise or discard proposals that do not hold up.\n\nThen test the design with appropriate users or other evidence. Record which conclusions come from research and which remain assumptions.\n\nInclude review, correction, and maintenance when assessing effort. Producing a screen quickly is one part of the work, not a complete measure of the design process.\n\n## Пов'язані терміни\n\n- [AI-native Design](/ua/glossary/ai-native-design.html)\n- [AI Prototyping](/ua/glossary/ai-prototyping.html)\n- [Design Harness](/ua/glossary/design-harness.html)\n- [AI in UX Research](/ua/glossary/ai-ux-research.html)\n\n## Джерела\n\n- [Design Process Isn't Dead, It's Compressed, NN/g](https://www.nngroup.com/articles/design-process-isnt-dead/)\n- [AI Prototyping in Real Design Contexts, NN/g](https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ai-prototyping/)",
